WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.267 --> 00:00:03.534
-Donald Trump
has appealed a ruling

00:00:03.534 --> 00:00:05.667
in the case over his
stolen top-secret documents

00:00:05.667 --> 00:00:06.901
directly to the Supreme Court --

00:00:06.901 --> 00:00:09.300
and specifically
Justice Clarence Thomas,

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:11.634
whose wife, Ginni Thomas,
has been implicated

00:00:11.634 --> 00:00:14.634
in Trump's attempted coup
and whom Trump praised publicly

00:00:14.634 --> 00:00:17.267
at a recent rally --
posing a major test

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:19.567
for the strength
of our constitutional system.

00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:21.901
Also in an equally
important story,

00:00:21.901 --> 00:00:23.167
Trump reportedly complained

00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:25.701
about how awful
Rudy Giuliani's [bleep] smelled.

00:00:25.701 --> 00:00:29.067
Those two stories
are both important.

00:00:29.067 --> 00:00:30.234
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.234 --> 00:00:32.300
They are the same level
of importance.

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:34.334
We're going to talk
about them the same amount

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:36.000
because they matter the same.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.367
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.367 --> 00:00:41.400
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:43.167 --> 00:00:45.601
♪♪

00:00:45.601 --> 00:00:49.300
Every so often a story comes
along that makes us throw out

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:51.400
everything we are planning
on doing that night on the show,

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:52.534
a blockbuster story

00:00:52.534 --> 00:00:54.300
of monumental consequence
to the nation.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.400
It happened many times
during the Trump presidency --

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:59.801
the Mueller investigation, two
impeachments, an attempted coup.

00:00:59.801 --> 00:01:02.434
And look, I don't want to say
that our audience expects

00:01:02.434 --> 00:01:04.567
or needs us
to provide this service,

00:01:04.567 --> 00:01:06.167
but we feel a moral obligation

00:01:06.167 --> 00:01:07.634
to bring you
the biggest stories of the day.

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:10.100
Because for many people,
let's face it,

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:13.801
and I don't say this lightly,
we are their Walter Cronkite.

00:01:13.801 --> 00:01:19.000
People trust us to bring them
the stories that matter most

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:24.734
and to do it with poise
and moral clarity and gravitas.

00:01:24.734 --> 00:01:27.367
In fact, Alex,
this one is so big,

00:01:27.367 --> 00:01:29.300
can we go to black and white?

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:30.634
Great.

00:01:30.634 --> 00:01:32.567
And, uh, cigarette, please?

00:01:32.567 --> 00:01:34.100
Thank you very much.

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:36.267
Alright, let's do it.

00:01:38.067 --> 00:01:41.267
Tonight we begin our show
with a story of immense

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:43.634
significance to the future
of our nation.

00:01:43.634 --> 00:01:46.601
It involves
a deeply corrupt ex-president

00:01:46.601 --> 00:01:49.701
who poses an existential threat
to democracy

00:01:49.701 --> 00:01:51.734
and the accomplices
around him who aid

00:01:51.734 --> 00:01:53.734
and abet
his criminal lawlessness.

00:01:53.734 --> 00:01:55.567
According to
a blockbuster tell-all

00:01:55.567 --> 00:01:57.367
by "New York Times" reporter
Maggie Haberman...

00:02:02.167 --> 00:02:06.767
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.767 --> 00:02:09.334
Alex, I think we can bring
the color back now.

00:02:11.167 --> 00:02:12.968
That's right -- Trump loudly

00:02:12.968 --> 00:02:15.300
complained about
his lawyer's stinky dumps.

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:16.434
According to the book...

00:02:31.834 --> 00:02:33.734
This is one of those
shocking stories

00:02:33.734 --> 00:02:35.734
you also definitely
could have predicted.

00:02:35.734 --> 00:02:38.067
No one thinks
Rudy is making good smells.

00:02:38.067 --> 00:02:39.367
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.367 --> 00:02:41.067
It's why he's constantly voted
New York mayor

00:02:41.067 --> 00:02:42.901
at least likely to have
his own fragrance.

00:02:42.901 --> 00:02:44.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.267 --> 00:02:46.200
You know who's most likely?
Eric Adams.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:48.834
I mean, cologne is probably
the solution

00:02:48.834 --> 00:02:50.200
to the trash problem for him.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:52.033
"I know that garbage
on the street smells bad.

00:02:52.033 --> 00:02:53.200
That's why I never
leave the house

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:54.567
without putting on
some Swagger."

00:02:54.567 --> 00:02:56.467
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.467 --> 00:03:01.033
So I'm not surprised Rudy makes
bad smells, but I am surprised

00:03:01.033 --> 00:03:04.334
it's so bad that Trump
complained about it.

00:03:04.334 --> 00:03:07.167
I mean, all Trump consumes
are Big Macs and Diet Cokes.

00:03:07.167 --> 00:03:09.100
He probably has
one bowel movement a week

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:11.000
that looks like
the scene from "Jurassic Park."

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:13.167
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.167 --> 00:03:15.133
And of course,
even as he was running

00:03:15.133 --> 00:03:16.801
for the most important job
in the world,

00:03:16.801 --> 00:03:18.734
that was what Trump
was preoccupied with.

00:03:18.734 --> 00:03:20.868
I'm sure it happened
after he won, too.

00:03:20.868 --> 00:03:22.434
"Mr. President, North Korea

00:03:22.434 --> 00:03:24.100
just launched a nuclear missile
into the --"

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:26.234
"God damn it, Rudy!

00:03:26.234 --> 00:03:27.601
What the hell
did you do it here?

00:03:27.601 --> 00:03:31.534
It's Air Force One,
not Air Force number two!"

00:03:31.534 --> 00:03:35.167
I'm guessing the reason
Trump reacted so fast

00:03:35.167 --> 00:03:37.534
was so he could
beat Rudy to the punch,

00:03:37.534 --> 00:03:40.033
because Rudy definitely
has the vibe of a

00:03:40.033 --> 00:03:42.667
"don't go in there"
kind of guy.

00:03:42.667 --> 00:03:44.100
I mean,
Rudy immediately confesses

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:45.334
to everything
without prompting.

00:03:45.334 --> 00:03:46.701
I'm shocked
he didn't do it on TV.

00:03:46.701 --> 00:03:48.834
Remember all those
televised confessions?

00:03:48.834 --> 00:03:51.834
-Did our State Department ask
you to go on a mission for them?

00:03:51.834 --> 00:03:53.033
-They did.

00:03:53.033 --> 00:03:55.868
And you know who I did it
at the request of?

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:56.968
The State Department.

00:03:56.968 --> 00:03:59.167
It's all here.
Right here.

00:03:59.167 --> 00:04:01.467
-So you did ask Ukraine
to look into Joe Biden?

00:04:01.467 --> 00:04:02.834
-Of course I did.

00:04:02.834 --> 00:04:04.834
-"Did you drink an entire bottle
of scotch with dinner?"

00:04:04.834 --> 00:04:05.868
"Sure!"

00:04:05.868 --> 00:04:07.601
"And did you eat
an entire prime rib?"

00:04:07.601 --> 00:04:08.634
"Yes!"

00:04:08.634 --> 00:04:09.467
"And how did your system

00:04:09.467 --> 00:04:10.501
react to that combination?"

00:04:10.501 --> 00:04:11.701
"Not well!"

00:04:11.701 --> 00:04:14.334
"And did you destroy
the airplane lavatory?"

00:04:14.334 --> 00:04:15.300
-Of course I did.

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:17.367
-I'm not --
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.367 --> 00:04:19.000
I'm not exaggerating
when I tell you

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:20.634
that this is
the most important story

00:04:20.634 --> 00:04:22.367
we have ever covered
on this show.

00:04:22.367 --> 00:04:25.434
This is our Watergate.

00:04:25.434 --> 00:04:28.701
So many pieces of the puzzle

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:31.200
are finally falling into place.

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:33.834
For example, now we know

00:04:33.834 --> 00:04:35.968
why Trump's always
complaining about toilets.

00:04:35.968 --> 00:04:39.300
-People are flushing toilets
10 times, 15 times.

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:45.267
Sinks, toilets, and showers.

00:04:45.267 --> 00:04:48.367
You don't get any water.
We won't talk about toilets.

00:04:48.367 --> 00:04:49.434
But, you know a...

00:04:49.434 --> 00:04:51.934
tink, tink, tink.

00:04:51.934 --> 00:04:53.400
10, 15 --

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:54.667
but we don't talk about that.

00:04:54.667 --> 00:04:57.834
Sinks, right? Showers.

00:04:57.834 --> 00:04:59.634
And what goes with a sink
and a shower?

00:05:02.167 --> 00:05:04.234
10 times, right? 10 times.

00:05:04.234 --> 00:05:05.901
I won't talk about the fact

00:05:05.901 --> 00:05:08.701
that people have to flush
their toilet 15 times.

00:05:08.701 --> 00:05:10.434
-Now, in the past,
when I've heard that,

00:05:10.434 --> 00:05:12.234
my reaction has been,
even for Donald Trump,

00:05:12.234 --> 00:05:13.901
that seems like
a lot of flushes.

00:05:13.901 --> 00:05:17.267
But now I know
there was a second pooper.

00:05:17.267 --> 00:05:20.434
Also, I want to emphasize
that according to the book,

00:05:20.434 --> 00:05:24.634
this happened in 2016 and Rudy
still went to work for Trump

00:05:24.634 --> 00:05:26.367
for six more years.

00:05:26.367 --> 00:05:27.634
I don't know about you guys,

00:05:27.634 --> 00:05:29.701
but if my boss made it a point
to loudly complain

00:05:29.701 --> 00:05:31.701
about how bad the bathroom
smelled after I used it

00:05:31.701 --> 00:05:33.067
so that everyone else
could hear,

00:05:33.067 --> 00:05:35.133
my response would not be
"I am willing

00:05:35.133 --> 00:05:36.701
to go to jail for this man,"

00:05:36.701 --> 00:05:39.801
because let's make it clear --
Rudy isn't the bad guy here.

00:05:39.801 --> 00:05:41.767
Sure, he can make
some dietary adjustments,

00:05:41.767 --> 00:05:43.100
but you reach a certain age

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:44.133
and it's going to be
what it's going to be.

00:05:44.133 --> 00:05:46.200
Trump is the bad guy here.

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:48.267
Being Trump's lawyer
is the worst job in the world.

00:05:48.267 --> 00:05:49.267
You don't get paid.

00:05:49.267 --> 00:05:50.300
You're constantly
exposing yourself

00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:51.634
to criminal charges.

00:05:51.634 --> 00:05:54.767
And he loudly complains
about your bathroom smells.

00:05:54.767 --> 00:05:57.167
"Rudy, you're a lawyer.
Could you help my toilet out?

00:05:57.167 --> 00:05:58.934
It's trying to file
a restraining order

00:05:58.934 --> 00:06:00.167
against your butthole.

00:06:00.167 --> 00:06:02.067
[ Laughter ]

00:06:02.067 --> 00:06:04.534
Do you guys hear what I said
about Rudy?

00:06:04.534 --> 00:06:06.501
Did everybody
on the plane hear it?"

00:06:06.501 --> 00:06:09.434
[ Laughter ]

00:06:09.434 --> 00:06:11.300
We should be done
with this story by now,

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:12.934
and yet I still have
so many questions.

00:06:12.934 --> 00:06:14.667
Like, for example,

00:06:14.667 --> 00:06:16.567
they make it sound like
it was a regular thing.

00:06:16.567 --> 00:06:19.767
Why was Trump always going into
the bathroom right after Rudy?

00:06:19.767 --> 00:06:21.901
Was it just a revolving door

00:06:21.901 --> 00:06:25.667
where these two Big Mac
receptacles go back and forth,

00:06:25.667 --> 00:06:28.033
just absolutely wrecking
the airplane bathroom

00:06:28.033 --> 00:06:28.968
until they landed?

00:06:28.968 --> 00:06:30.467
"Knock, knock, anyone in there?"

00:06:30.467 --> 00:06:31.801
"You know it's me, boss!

00:06:31.801 --> 00:06:34.868
[ Laughter ]

00:06:34.868 --> 00:06:36.200
I came in when you came out."

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:38.734
"Well, it's time again
for me, Rudy."

00:06:40.234 --> 00:06:42.868
[ Laughter ]

00:06:42.868 --> 00:06:44.300
I don't want to be
overdramatic here,

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:46.367
but we need a congressional
investigation into this.

00:06:46.367 --> 00:06:47.801
Liz Cheney needs to work this

00:06:47.801 --> 00:06:49.501
into the next January six
hearing.

00:06:49.501 --> 00:06:51.467
And lest you think
I'm being silly, remember,

00:06:51.467 --> 00:06:54.501
they did do an entire segment
at the hearings

00:06:54.501 --> 00:06:56.501
about how Rudy was drunk
on election night.

00:06:56.501 --> 00:06:59.033
-Was there anyone in that
conversation who,

00:06:59.033 --> 00:07:02.601
in your observation,
had had too much to drink?

00:07:04.667 --> 00:07:07.634
-Um, Mayor Giuliani.

00:07:07.634 --> 00:07:09.234
-"And how did you know that

00:07:09.234 --> 00:07:11.767
Rudy was at the White House
that night?"

00:07:11.767 --> 00:07:14.634
-"Uh, there was police tape
on one of the bathroom doors.

00:07:14.634 --> 00:07:17.734
[ Laughter ]

00:07:19.901 --> 00:07:22.601
Also, this mask
isn't because of COVID."

00:07:22.601 --> 00:07:25.801
[ Laughter ]

00:07:28.501 --> 00:07:29.934
Now, as much as I'd love

00:07:29.934 --> 00:07:31.968
to spend the rest of the show
on this story,

00:07:31.968 --> 00:07:35.000
and believe me, we thought about
going live tonight to cover it,

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:39.133
but the network did not respond
to our many e-mails,

00:07:39.133 --> 00:07:40.300
there are, I guess, some other

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:41.467
less important stories
in the news.

00:07:41.467 --> 00:07:43.167
For example, the investigation

00:07:43.167 --> 00:07:45.000
into all those
top-secret documents

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:46.234
Trump stole
from the White House

00:07:46.234 --> 00:07:47.868
and stashed in the basement of

00:07:47.868 --> 00:07:50.400
his Palm Beach
resort/luxury morgue.

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:52.267
And you can rest assured,

00:07:52.267 --> 00:07:54.934
you can rest assured
there is no possible connection

00:07:54.934 --> 00:07:57.400
between Trump's handling
of official government records

00:07:57.400 --> 00:07:59.167
and the toilet story
we just told you about.

00:07:59.167 --> 00:08:02.100
-Staff members at
the White House residence

00:08:02.100 --> 00:08:06.467
discovered wads of printed paper
in a clogged toilet

00:08:06.467 --> 00:08:08.267
and believe that
former President Trump

00:08:08.267 --> 00:08:10.801
was trying to flush documents.

00:08:10.801 --> 00:08:12.868
-In her new book,
Maggie Haberman

00:08:12.868 --> 00:08:15.767
of "The New York Times" confirms
a habit of the former president

00:08:15.767 --> 00:08:18.133
that wasn't just unhealthy
for the White House plumbing,

00:08:18.133 --> 00:08:20.367
it was bad
for the presidency as well.

00:08:20.367 --> 00:08:22.367
And she's got the photos
to prove it.

00:08:22.367 --> 00:08:25.267
-Damn it, we can't get away
from this toilet story!

00:08:25.267 --> 00:08:26.567
[ Laughter ]

00:08:26.567 --> 00:08:29.467
Every time I think I'm out,
they flush me back in.

00:08:29.467 --> 00:08:31.934
Even more shocking to me
is that both these stories

00:08:31.934 --> 00:08:33.400
are in the same book

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:35.000
by "New York Times" reporter
Maggie Haberman.

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:37.567
She wrote a deeply reported
600-page tell-all

00:08:37.567 --> 00:08:38.801
about the
most dangerous president

00:08:38.801 --> 00:08:40.234
in modern American history.

00:08:40.234 --> 00:08:43.367
And to do it, she had to spend
a significant amount of time

00:08:43.367 --> 00:08:45.133
investigating
the weird toilet habits

00:08:45.133 --> 00:08:46.567
of the grossest freaks on Earth.

00:08:46.567 --> 00:08:49.534
Toilets have never played
such a large role

00:08:49.534 --> 00:08:50.601
in American history before.

00:08:50.601 --> 00:08:52.033
I mean, just look
at the index.

00:08:52.033 --> 00:08:54.067
Here in the mentions of
Mike Pence in the book,

00:08:54.067 --> 00:08:55.968
and here are the mentions
for toilets.

00:08:55.968 --> 00:08:59.000
[ Laughter ]

00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:03.968
I mean, that's it, I prom--
No more --

00:09:03.968 --> 00:09:06.200
No more toilet stuff!

00:09:06.200 --> 00:09:08.133
The point is,
Trump's habit of destroying

00:09:08.133 --> 00:09:09.701
or stealing official
government records,

00:09:09.701 --> 00:09:11.100
including top-secret documents

00:09:11.100 --> 00:09:13.467
with the most sensitive
classified information,

00:09:13.467 --> 00:09:16.501
is now under a very intense
federal criminal investigation.

00:09:16.501 --> 00:09:18.634
So naturally,
Trump is once again

00:09:18.634 --> 00:09:20.400
trying to manipulate
the courts to help him.

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:22.834
In fact, now he's going all
the way to the Supreme Court.

00:09:22.834 --> 00:09:25.801
And in particular, his appeal
was addressed to a justice

00:09:25.801 --> 00:09:28.601
who is very obviously
and blatantly compromised

00:09:28.601 --> 00:09:30.534
in a way
that should disqualify him.

00:09:30.534 --> 00:09:32.234
-We have
some breaking news to report

00:09:32.234 --> 00:09:33.667
in the criminal investigation

00:09:33.667 --> 00:09:36.567
into Donald Trump's handling
of classified documents.

00:09:36.567 --> 00:09:39.734
Attorneys for the ex-president
made an attempt to block

00:09:39.734 --> 00:09:43.801
DOJ's criminal investigation
by asking the US Supreme Court

00:09:43.801 --> 00:09:46.467
to reverse a ruling
by an appeals court

00:09:46.467 --> 00:09:49.300
that gives the DOJ access
to classified documents

00:09:49.300 --> 00:09:51.000
that were seized at Mar-a-Lago.

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:53.667
-Notably, this request
from Trump's team

00:09:53.667 --> 00:09:56.434
does go directly to
Justice Clarence Thomas.

00:09:56.434 --> 00:10:00.133
-Clarence Thomas' wife,
who is a lawyer,

00:10:00.133 --> 00:10:02.834
urged Republicans in state
legislatures around the country

00:10:02.834 --> 00:10:05.667
to change the outcome
of the presidential election.

00:10:05.667 --> 00:10:08.267
-No Supreme Court justice
in history

00:10:08.267 --> 00:10:12.267
has ever been more
publicly compromised

00:10:12.267 --> 00:10:16.067
by the conduct of a relative
than Clarence Thomas.

00:10:16.067 --> 00:10:20.400
But today, Clarence Thomas
did not recuse himself

00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:23.467
when Donald Trump's lawyers
filed their appeal

00:10:23.467 --> 00:10:27.734
to the Supreme Court
directly to Clarence Thomas.

00:10:27.734 --> 00:10:30.234
-That's right -- Trump's appeal
went directly to Clarence Thomas

00:10:30.234 --> 00:10:33.300
because Clarence Thomas
is the justice with jurisdiction

00:10:33.300 --> 00:10:35.334
over the 11th Circuit Court
of Appeals,

00:10:35.334 --> 00:10:37.534
which issued the ruling
Trump is appealing.

00:10:37.534 --> 00:10:39.834
And Thomas did not immediately
recuse himself,

00:10:39.834 --> 00:10:41.033
which is obviously insane.

00:10:41.033 --> 00:10:42.634
His wife, Ginni Thomas,
tried to help Trump

00:10:42.634 --> 00:10:44.501
overthrow
a presidential election.

00:10:44.501 --> 00:10:47.400
You can't pretend like that
just didn't happen.

00:10:47.400 --> 00:10:48.667
That would be like
using the bathroom

00:10:48.667 --> 00:10:49.701
right after Rudy Giuliani

00:10:49.701 --> 00:10:54.000
and not saying
anything about it.

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:55.200
I said we wouldn't
bring it up again

00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:57.567
and we brought it up again.
I'm very sorry.

00:10:57.567 --> 00:10:59.467
Seriously, Clarence Thomas
shouldn't even be on the bench,

00:10:59.467 --> 00:11:02.467
let alone ruling on cases
directly involving the guy

00:11:02.467 --> 00:11:05.367
his wife teamed up with to
orchestrate an attempted coup.

00:11:05.367 --> 00:11:08.133
For one thing, I seriously doubt
they never talked about it.

00:11:08.133 --> 00:11:09.701
Can you imagine
any married person

00:11:09.701 --> 00:11:11.467
saying with a straight face,
"Oh, no,

00:11:11.467 --> 00:11:15.434
I've never heard any of
my spouse's insane opinions"?

00:11:15.434 --> 00:11:17.133
Thomas involving himself
in this ruling

00:11:17.133 --> 00:11:19.100
is even more ludicrous
given that his wife, Ginni,

00:11:19.100 --> 00:11:21.834
just testified to the January
Six Committee last week.

00:11:21.834 --> 00:11:24.100
During that testimony,
she actually stood by her belief

00:11:24.100 --> 00:11:25.601
that the 2020 election
was stolen.

00:11:25.601 --> 00:11:28.801
And then Trump praised her for
it at a rally over the weekend.

00:11:28.801 --> 00:11:31.133
-Ginni Thomas,
the conservative activist

00:11:31.133 --> 00:11:33.667
and wife of Supreme Court
Justice Clarence Thomas,

00:11:33.667 --> 00:11:36.400
met today with the January
Six Select House Committee.

00:11:36.400 --> 00:11:38.968
-We are told
that she cooperated,

00:11:38.968 --> 00:11:41.534
that she answered
every question.

00:11:41.534 --> 00:11:46.501
But Chairman Bennie Thompson
has also told reporters

00:11:46.501 --> 00:11:50.667
that she still believes
the election was stolen, Jake.

00:11:50.667 --> 00:11:53.667
So after everything we know,

00:11:53.667 --> 00:11:57.534
Ginni Thomas is still
an election denier.

00:11:57.534 --> 00:12:02.033
-I would like to thank a great
woman named Ginni Thomas.

00:12:02.033 --> 00:12:04.334
Do you know Ginni Thomas?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:04.334 --> 00:12:07.801
She's a great woman,
the wife of a great man --

00:12:07.801 --> 00:12:11.534
Justice Clarence Thomas --
for her courage and strength.

00:12:11.534 --> 00:12:15.400
She said that she still believes
the 2020 election was stolen.

00:12:15.400 --> 00:12:18.133
She didn't say, "Oh, well,
I'd like not to get involved.

00:12:18.133 --> 00:12:19.901
Of course, it was
a wonderful election."

00:12:19.901 --> 00:12:22.300
It was a rigged
and stolen election.

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:24.200
-I do like Trump's impressions
of other people

00:12:24.200 --> 00:12:25.400
because they're all the same

00:12:25.400 --> 00:12:26.901
regardless of who
he's talking about.

00:12:26.901 --> 00:12:29.300
It doesn't matter if it's
Joe Biden or Ginni Thomas.

00:12:29.300 --> 00:12:31.567
I'd love to see
his SNL audition.

00:12:31.567 --> 00:12:33.934
"Next, I'll be doing
my Harry Styles impression.

00:12:33.934 --> 00:12:35.334
Okay, here we go.
[ Clears throat ]

00:12:35.334 --> 00:12:36.968
Hi, my name is Harry Styles.

00:12:36.968 --> 00:12:40.167
I...I do songs
and spit on Chris Pine."

00:12:40.167 --> 00:12:42.501
[ Laughter ]

00:12:42.501 --> 00:12:44.434
But again, let's step back
and process

00:12:44.434 --> 00:12:45.834
the order of things here.

00:12:45.834 --> 00:12:47.701
Clarence Thomas' spouse
urged lawmakers

00:12:47.701 --> 00:12:49.901
in several states
to overturn the 2020 election.

00:12:49.901 --> 00:12:51.534
She texted Trump's
chief of staff

00:12:51.534 --> 00:12:52.968
and urged him not to concede.

00:12:52.968 --> 00:12:55.601
She then repeated those lies
to the January Six Committee.

00:12:55.601 --> 00:12:58.667
Trump then praised her and her
husband at a political rally,

00:12:58.667 --> 00:13:01.901
and now her husband is ruling
on a case involving Trump's

00:13:01.901 --> 00:13:04.968
potentially criminal handling of
classified documents.

00:13:04.968 --> 00:13:07.234
If that isn't
a brazen conflict of interest,

00:13:07.234 --> 00:13:08.334
I don't know what is.

00:13:08.334 --> 00:13:10.000
This is a conflict of interest

00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:11.934
on the level of finding out
the Mets' pitching staff

00:13:11.934 --> 00:13:15.467
we're secretly all Braves fans,
which would explain a lot.

00:13:15.467 --> 00:13:17.767
Look, I don't want to pick
on the Mets,

00:13:17.767 --> 00:13:19.501
but they're the only team
in the history of baseball

00:13:19.501 --> 00:13:21.901
that could win 100 games
and still make their fans

00:13:21.901 --> 00:13:24.601
feel absolutely
[bleep] miserable.

00:13:24.601 --> 00:13:27.567
And maybe this Mets situation
doesn't affect all of you,

00:13:27.567 --> 00:13:32.200
but I somehow work with
every single fan of the Mets,

00:13:32.200 --> 00:13:34.601
and they've been walking around
all day this week

00:13:34.601 --> 00:13:38.200
like they just used the bathroom
after Rudy Giuliani.

00:13:38.200 --> 00:13:44.033
Which is ironic because we got
a few Rudys on the crew.

00:13:44.033 --> 00:13:45.834
You know who you are.

00:13:47.968 --> 00:13:50.234
[ Laughter ]

00:13:50.234 --> 00:13:54.567
As gross and unimportant
as the Rudy toilet story is,

00:13:54.567 --> 00:13:56.601
it's both, A, very funny

00:13:56.601 --> 00:13:59.701
and, B, an example
of the kinds of humiliation

00:13:59.701 --> 00:14:02.267
the people in Trump's orbit are
willing to endure to serve him.

00:14:02.267 --> 00:14:04.067
And that orbit now includes
the spouse

00:14:04.067 --> 00:14:06.667
of a Supreme Court justice
who is poised to rule

00:14:06.667 --> 00:14:09.200
on a very serious
federal criminal investigation

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:11.033
into Trump's handling
of classified documents.

00:14:11.033 --> 00:14:12.300
Trump has destroyed
the integrity

00:14:12.300 --> 00:14:14.167
of our nation's institutions,

00:14:14.167 --> 00:14:16.000
just as Rudy has destroyed
our nation's --

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:19.434
-Toilets!
-This...

00:14:19.434 --> 00:14:20.667
has been "A Closer Look."

00:14:20.667 --> 00:14:24.400
♪♪

